    Both are 60dp, and they are two resources rather than one shared value because each
    provider states its own floor and the two are free to diverge — they coincide today
    because the form is the same two lines of type in both: a 20sp name and a 12sp
    supporting line, each occupying about 1.3× its font size in a `TextView`, inside 8dp
    of padding, come to 57.6dp. 60dp is that rounded up to a whole number, and it lands
    inside the 40–60dp a single launcher cell reports on most devices, which is what
    makes a one-cell-tall placement reachable at all.

    Unlike the placement sizes above, a `minResizeHeight` is never a size the widget is
    given — only the floor a launcher measures a drag against — so it does not have to
    be a whole number of cells, and neither of these is.
